-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Alien 8
  Publisher   Ultimate, 1985
  Version     1.1

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Alien 8 (1985)(Ultimate Play The Game).z80
  MD5         91a07828482c3e9b0fb76564abe3fe87

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Every figure painted in its own colours: the robot in white and
              blue with red, fires in yellow and orange on red, the doorway
              arches blue-grey, and the droids, cryogenic chambers, items and
              hazards each in their own colours, on a dark grey floor; the
              room walls keep the original's ink. No outlines added. Source:
              Enhanced colours: Jon Attree, painted over the original game's
              own figures.

  Pace        original (-1.71% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless; 18 paired
              trials, default and Enhanced, three scenes, three R and raster
              phases each; player state, inputs and beeper writes equal to the
              original at every update; one cold redraw adds up to 117.5 ms)

  Changes     1.0: review build, not published: figures as Next sprites, the
              original's order and masks, Sinclair's 48K ROM as the whole alt
              ROM, translated cheats.
              1.1: Enhanced colours on every figure, painted by Jon Attree,
              and the dark grey floor; steady walking pace recalibrated to the
              original's.

  Note        Keys: on the game's menu 1 keyboard, 2 Kempston, 3 cursor or 4
              Interface II joystick, 5 directional control, then 0 to start.
              The default is the original game's look, its figures moved onto
              Next sprites, with Sinclair's whole 48K ROM so it runs on
              NextZXOS 26.11. Enhanced paints every figure in its own colours
              on a dark grey floor; off by default. The original 48K game with
              its beeper sound; fits a 1MB Next. Known issues: entering a room
              cold or losing a life redraws the room up to about 0.12 seconds
              slower than the original, made up over the next few seconds
              (death stretches up to 5 percent slower, then up to 2.5 percent
              faster); steady play is within 2 percent of the original. With
              Infinite lives and Start 10 lives both on, the lives counter
              shows 00 although you have 10. Missing: not reached in testing:
              natural play to the end, joysticks; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  No time-out
   3  Immunity
   4  Freeze objects
   5  Mega jumps
   6  Start 10 lives
   7  Time 999
   8  One room goal

  The archive's POKEs translated to this exact 48K release and checked to
  survive a restart; One room goal sets the original's real target (24 rooms,
  stored as BCD, not the archive's 36); the archive's inventory POKEs are
  unsafe on this release and left out.

